    The compiled checker reads a self-typed trait's self as the implementing type from its F-bound, keeps the signatures plain, and refuses an extender at another type

    The team's specification typed self as the enclosing trait, and as its intersection with the listed types only under a comprises clause, so the checker refused 29 of the library's default bodies that return or pass self where the trait's own parameter is declared, the team's minimal complete definitions of its orders, algebra and arrays; nothing checked that a type extending such a trait is an instance of its argument. Under P-146 (way 6) self in the method bodies is C[\X\] & X while the signatures keep C[\X\], since the 2019 account of overloading assumes declared types with no type parameter inside an intersection, and a declaration extending C[\A\] must be an A, as Scala requires a class's self type to conform to those it inherits; by the coordinator's default, on the review list, a mixin's parameter bounded by a self-typed trait it extends counts as its self parameter, which keeps the team's Containment mixins valid. Climb batch 14's rung S, from wip/rung-self-type; row 710 opened.

